diff --git a/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js b/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
index a89a88e783e3d82cd9d2a43366fbf58948913784..ad08aa7d525ead7e1a1edbc22deab4f1d9f17525 100644
--- a/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
+++ b/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@ gettext("<p>Open <span class='knopfwort'>Tasks</span> and tap <span class='knopf
 gettext("<p>Open Settings → Country &amp; holidays → <b>Time zone management</b>. Enable the required areas and choose a manual zone or automatic detection with a manual fallback. Automatic sources use available fresh phone, GPS or IP information; an IP/VPN location can differ from your actual location. A country or UTC offset alone does not identify a zone. Detect now previews a result; Refresh applies it. Save commits choices; Cancel discards the dialog draft. The operating-system clock and zone are never changed.</p><p>Assign a known zone to a contact to show its local time. For calendar and task display choose your own, the contact’s or the original zone. A linked individual entry offers <b>Keep instant</b> for another display or <b>Plan local time</b> to deliberately change its instant. Normal editors show the saved input zone. A nonexistent daylight-saving time is rejected; a repeated time requires the earlier or later occurrence. All-day dates, floating times and opaque recurrence data keep their source meaning. UTC/TZID, seconds, identities and recurrence exceptions are preserved during synchronization.</p>");
 gettext("<p>Open Settings → Import → <b>Lotus Organizer (.or6 / .csv) …</b> and select an OR6 file or CSV export. OR6 imports basic appointments, tasks, contacts and note text. Series, groups and other sections are skipped; layout, attachments, categories and alarms are not transferred. Read the import report. For CSV, export each desired section in Lotus using File → Export → Delimited ASCII/CSV, then import each file separately. The original is read only. The file limit is 32 MiB; ZIP imports also have entry and size limits.</p>");
 gettext("<p>Open a note or task and tap Print to use its current draft. Android offers the printer or Save as PDF. Cancelling returns to the editor. Time tracking has its own month/day print choices. Printing does not silently synchronize the entry.</p><p>Automatic print-icon visibility is on by default. Allow a short discovery delay for an advertised, reachable IPP/IPPS Wi-Fi printer. For PDF or other Android print services, turn this option off under Settings → Print; the print action then remains available.</p><p>Tap Version in Settings to open About. Installed version and actually published Notes version are separate; a desktop release number is not a Notes version. Offline, publication can be unavailable while the installed version remains visible. Check again retries; Open release appears for a newer published Notes version. Installation remains your choice.</p><figure class='notes-native-figure'><div class='notes-native-images'><img src='notes-native-about.png' alt='Native Android examples with invented data, cropped without retouching. Picture values and selections are examples.'></div><figcaption>Native Android examples with invented data, cropped without retouching. Picture values and selections are examples.</figcaption></figure><h3>Related Organizer pages</h3><p><b data-page='printing-and-saving-as-pdf' data-page-title='true' class='knopfwort'></b> · <b data-page='android-apk-install-update' data-page-title='true' class='knopfwort'></b></p>");
-gettext("<p>Open the <span class='knopfwort'>Import</span> tab. Android keeps every app's private database closed to other apps, so Magnolie Notes cannot simply look inside Samsung Notes, Google Keep or another notepad. Use an export file, an export folder, or Android's Share command instead.</p><h3>Choose one file</h3><ol class='schritte'><li>Tap <span class='knopfwort'>Choose file …</span>.</li><li>Select the export in Android's document picker.</li><li>Wait while <span class='knopfwort'>Reading …</span> is displayed.</li><li>Read the result before opening Notes.</li></ol><p>The picker initially allows every file type because Magnolie Notes examines the name and contents itself. A selected file may contain at most <b>64 MiB</b>. An unknown file can fall back to a plain-text note, so do not select a binary file merely because Android offers it.</p><h3>Choose a folder</h3><p><span class='knopfwort'>Choose folder …</span> reads suitable files in that folder and its subfolders. Text, Markdown, JSON, HTML, ENEX and supported ZIP-based exports are considered; unrelated suffixes and files over 64 MiB are skipped. Magnolie reads the selection immediately and does not remember access to the folder for later.</p><div class='achtung'><b>A complete desktop archive does not fit here</b>A <b>.magnolie</b> complete archive from Magnolie Organizer is deliberately rejected with <i>Complete archive import is not yet supported on this device.</i> Keep that archive for the desktop Organizer.</div>");
+gettext("<p>Open the <span class='knopfwort'>Import</span> tab. Android keeps every app's private database closed to other apps, so Magnolie Notes cannot simply look inside Samsung Notes, Google Keep or another notepad. Use an export file, an export folder, or Android's Share command instead.</p><h3>Choose one file</h3><ol class='schritte'><li>Tap <span class='knopfwort'>Choose file …</span>.</li><li>Select the export in Android's document picker.</li><li>Wait while <span class='knopfwort'>Reading …</span> is displayed.</li><li>Read the result before opening Notes.</li></ol><p>The file picker offers supported note exports. Magnolie Notes also checks the actual contents and rejects binary data or invalid UTF-8 text. A selected file is limited to <b>64 MiB</b>; a text file outside an archive is limited to <b>8 MiB</b>.</p><h3>Choose a folder</h3><p><span class='knopfwort'>Choose folder …</span> reads supported files in the selected folder and its subfolders. Unrelated file suffixes are ignored. One import is limited to <b>5,000 examined files and subfolders</b>, <b>5,000 notes</b>, <b>six subfolder levels</b>, <b>64 MiB of input files</b> and <b>64 MiB of decoded note content</b> altogether. If a supported file cannot be read completely or a limit is exceeded, the whole folder import stops without saving new notes. Split the export into smaller selections and try again. Folder access is not retained for later.</p><div class='achtung'><b>A complete desktop archive does not fit here</b>A <b>.magnolie</b> complete archive from Magnolie Organizer is deliberately rejected with <i>Complete archive import is not yet supported on this device.</i> Keep that archive for the desktop Organizer.</div>");
 gettext("<p>Open the <span class='knopfwort'>Recovery</span> tab and scroll below the trash to <b>Recovery journal</b>. It stores encrypted local snapshots inside Magnolie Notes. The default interval is weekly; choose <span class='knopfwort'>Off</span>, <span class='knopfwort'>6 hours</span>, <span class='knopfwort'>12 hours</span>, <span class='knopfwort'>Daily</span> or <span class='knopfwort'>Weekly</span>.</p><h3>Create and inspect a snapshot</h3><p><span class='knopfwort'>Snapshot now</span> creates a pinned manual snapshot. An unchanged snapshot with the same reason may be deduplicated within 15 minutes. Each row shows time, reason, area, size and summary. <span class='knopfwort'>Preview</span> shows the summary and technical hash and synchronization epoch; it is not a note-by-note content browser.</p><h3>Restore or remove</h3><p><span class='knopfwort'>Restore</span> asks for confirmation and creates a pre-restore snapshot before replacing app data. Restoring a bound Android contact may require a second confirmation if it has changed. <span class='knopfwort'>Delete</span> permanently removes the selected snapshot after confirmation.</p><p>Automatic retention keeps limited daily, monthly, pre-restore and pre-synchronization generations. The journal uses at most five percent of the file system or 512 MiB while trying to retain 256 MiB free. Pinned manual snapshots remain until you delete them.</p><div class='achtung'><b>This is not an external backup</b>Snapshots never enter Android cloud backup or device transfer. Clearing app data, uninstalling Magnolie Notes or losing the phone also loses this journal.</div>");
 gettext("<p>Open the <span class='knopfwort'>Tree</span> tab and scroll to <b>Magnolienbaum</b>. Give the phone a recognizable <span class='knopfwort'>Name of this branch</span>. Its identifier and fingerprint belong to this installation and are shown for comparison.</p><h3>Use a pairing file</h3><ol class='schritte'><li>In the desktop Organizer, open <span class='knopfwort'>Settings ▸ Magnolienbaum</span> and create a pairing file.</li><li>Bring it to the phone and tap <span class='knopfwort'>Open pairing file …</span>. The invitation is valid for <b>15 minutes</b>.</li><li>Alternatively paste its complete JSON under <span class='knopfwort'>Paste pairing text</span> and tap <span class='knopfwort'>OK</span>.</li><li>Read the result <i>Paired with …</i> before continuing.</li></ol><p><span class='knopfwort'>Create own pairing file …</span> starts Android's Share sheet with an invitation from the phone. It does not leave an ordinary file in Downloads.</p><h3>Search the local network</h3><p><span class='knopfwort'>Search the local network</span> lists answering branches with address and fingerprint. Tap <span class='knopfwort'>Connect</span>, compare the six-digit code on both devices and confirm <span class='knopfwort'>Code matches</span> only when every digit agrees.</p><div class='achtung'><b>QR pairing requires confirmation</b>After scanning, verify the displayed branch, address, and fingerprint before you confirm. You can still use the file, pasted pairing text, or local-network search. If a key has changed, remove the old connection first and compare the new fingerprint carefully.</div>");
 gettext("<p>Per-item change vectors distinguish later and concurrent changes. Concurrent changes preserve both versions; the loser receives a deterministic conflict-copy identity, so retrying does not create another copy.</p><h3>Attachment format 2</h3><p><b>format 2</b> supports JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, and PDF. Each file is at most <b>8 MiB</b>, with at most <b>64</b> per note. SHA-256, declared MIME, and file signature must agree.</p><p>Authenticated encrypted chunks support reuse and resume of missing ranges. Automatic transfer is Wi-Fi only; manual transfer may use the permitted RFCOMM fallback.</p><div class='achtung'><b>No silent loss</b>Invalid or unavailable files are reported; existing local attachments remain untouched.</div>");
